#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:1
msgid "BM Generation: Data Generation with a Fully Connected Boltzmann Machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:3
msgid ""
"This tutorial extends the RBM idea to a fully connected Boltzmann Machine"
" (BM), where all nodes are connected (not just across layers). It "
"demonstrates how to train a BM with a mixed KL-divergence + conditional "
"likelihood objective and generate samples from it. The system "
"architecture and sampling interface are introduced in "
"[Introduction](../introduction.md) and [Quick Start](../quickstart.md); "
"the theoretical background is covered in [Section 4.1: The Classic "
"Boltzmann Machine](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-"
"foundations-bm-overall.md). This tutorial focuses on what changes when "
"moving from an RBM to a BM: the new objective terms and conditional "
"sampling that a fully connected graph requires."
msgstr ""

