#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:55
msgid "The training objective combines two terms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:57
msgid ""
"**KL divergence**: encourages the model distribution to match the data "
"distribution (unsupervised generation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:58
msgid ""
"**Negative conditional likelihood (NCL)**: when part of the visible units"
" are designated as outputs (`num_output`), the model must reconstruct "
"those outputs given the rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:60
msgid "The combined objective is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:62
#, fuzzy, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal{L} = \\alpha \\cdot \\text{KL\\_divergence} + (1 - \\alpha) "
"\\cdot \\text{NCL}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"   \\mathcal{L} = \\alpha \\cdot \\text{KL\\_divergence} + (1 - \\alpha) "
"\\cdot \\text{NCL}\n"
"  "

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:66
#, fuzzy
msgid "where $\\alpha$ is set via `cost_param[\"alpha\"]`."
msgstr ""
"where $\\alpha$ is controlled by `cost_param[\"alpha\"]`, balancing "
"generation capability with conditional consistency."

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:68
msgid ""
"**Negative phase**: `bm_net.sample(worker)` draws a complete joint "
"visible+hidden state from the current BM distribution, approximating the "
"model distribution for the contrastive divergence objective."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:70
msgid ""
"**Positive phase**: the positive phase uses two conditional samplings per"
" batch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:72
msgid ""
"**Full conditional**: the entire input batch is fixed as the visible "
"layer, and the corresponding joint state is sampled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:73
msgid ""
"**Partial conditional**: only the non-output portion of the input "
"(`data[:, :-num_output]`) is fixed, and the output dimensions are sampled"
" freely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:75
msgid ""
"These two samplings compute the KL term and the NCL term respectively. A "
"cosine schedule with linear warmup stabilizes early training. Multi-"
"process sampling splits each batch across workers, running positive-phase"
" conditional sampling in parallel to accelerate the training loop. All "
"sampling operations are embedded in the PyTorch computation graph, "
"enabling end-to-end backpropagation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/bm_generation.md:77
msgid ""
"The `num_output` parameter designates which visible units are \"outputs\""
" (e.g. labels in a supervised setting), enabling conditional generation —"
" you can fix part of the visible units and let the model generate the "
"rest."
msgstr ""

